From ca1802c8a8e4ea089d68479b2bd5b2d5e089a23e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:28:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban reclaim: optional explicit-operator
 attribution on the reclaimed event

Worker core-update containment (t_f5ae6712b53e34e3, spec containment-spec.md
d2464db1) makes routine worker core updates idle-only; the only remaining
worker interruption is an explicit operator emergency
(state worker-core-update --interrupt-worker-runs). That route keeps the exact
reason "hermes-sync core update: restart-safe worker requeue" and must be
distinguishable in the durable reclaimed event for the 6h containment query.

- kanban reclaim gains --urgency-source {explicit_operator} and
  --interrupt-target <lowercase 40-hex>; both or neither, and only with the
  exact core-update requeue reason. Invalid/partial input refuses (exit 2)
  before any signal or claim change.
- kanban_db.reclaim_task(urgency_source=, interrupt_target=) validates the
  same way (ValueError before termination) and adds both fields to the
  existing reclaimed payload only when present. Legacy payload unchanged
  (absent = unknown attribution).
- hermes-sync probes `kanban reclaim --help` for both flags before any
  emergency signal; this commit ships first so every worker has the
  capability before containment activates.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_reclaim_attribution.py (parser -> cmd ->
event end to end, help lists both flags, partial/invalid refusal before
reclaim, DB-layer refusal before signalling, legacy payload unchanged).
